# EXTENSION to patrol_brique_incumbent_rdb3_seeds.jobs — take both arms to
# TWELVE seeds, and PRE-REGISTER the read-out before any of it is scored.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. Issue #56 sized the original six-run design: at five seeds it
# can reject on 1 of its 64 outcomes, and that one needs seed 16 to go mute at
# rdb=1.0 while seed 16's only observation reports (v17_pre42, 0.794). The
# first extension took both arms to eight seeds. #56's follow-up then showed
# that eight only works if the assumption behind it holds exactly:
#
#     realized rdb=1.0 count at 8 seeds   Fisher    paired (McNemar)
#         1                               0.0014    0.0156
#         2  <- what the 8-seed size assumed  0.0070    0.0312
#         3                               0.0256    0.0625  FAILS
#         4                               0.0769    0.1250  FAILS
#
# The paired reading survives only to b <= 2 — the assumed value itself, zero
# margin. ONE extra reporter among the four unrun rdb=1.0 cells puts it back at
# 0.0625, the identical failure the extension was bought to fix (~1 in 3 by the
# Jeffreys predictive, which is a modelling statement, not a measurement).
#
# scripts/design_power.py --size 8 10 12 14 --measured 2/4, i.e. sized against a
# TRUE rdb=1.0 rate double the measured one:
#
#     seeds  new runs  assumed  unpaired   paired
#         8        12      4/8    0.0769     0.1250
#        10        16     5/10    0.0325OK   0.0625
#        12        20     6/12    0.0137OK   0.0312OK   <- first size that survives
#
# Twelve seeds is where the primary reading still rejects if the comparison arm
# turns out to report at HALF its seeds instead of a quarter. That is insurance
# against the one assumption neither arm has ever tested — exchangeability of
# seeds WITHIN a scenario (§12.146 tested transfer ACROSS scenarios, and found
# none).
#
# ============ THE READ-OUT, FIXED NOW, BEFORE ANY CELL IS SCORED ============
# PRIMARY: exact McNemar over the seeds present in BOTH arms. The design is
#   paired by construction — seed is the nuisance variable being blocked — so
#   the paired test is the one that matches it.
# SECONDARY: Fisher, reported always and never as a rescue. Reporting whichever
#   of the two happens to clear 0.05 is test-shopping, and this file exists
#   because the project keeps having to retract underpowered readings.
# NO TEST AT ALL if any rdb=3.0 cell comes back mute: "3.0 splits too" is
#   settled descriptively by the first mute cell, and a Fisher p from this
#   design would not be a null result.
# LABELS come from scripts/reporting_channel.py (both checkpoints; a run whose
#   checkpoints disagree is SPLIT and is dropped, not silently counted).
# ===========================================================================
#
#     arm       12-15            16      17-19        20-23
#     rdb=3.0   v18-v21 (queued) v22     v24,v25,v26  v30,v32,v34,v36
#     rdb=1.0   v7,v10,v11,v12   v23     v27,v28,v29  v31,v33,v35,v37
#
# Chained behind the original queue, not launched beside it: two live queues
# contend for the same cores. No cohort/ file is touched, so the freeze holds
# and all twenty-four cells stay comparable.
patrol_brique_v24_rdb3_seed17  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 17 --reward root_done_bonus=3.0
patrol_brique_v25_rdb3_seed18  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 18 --reward root_done_bonus=3.0
patrol_brique_v26_rdb3_seed19  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 19 --reward root_done_bonus=3.0
patrol_brique_v27_rdb1_seed17  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 17
patrol_brique_v28_rdb1_seed18  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 18
patrol_brique_v29_rdb1_seed19  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 19
patrol_brique_v30_rdb3_seed20  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 20 --reward root_done_bonus=3.0
patrol_brique_v31_rdb1_seed20  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 20
patrol_brique_v32_rdb3_seed21  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 21 --reward root_done_bonus=3.0
patrol_brique_v33_rdb1_seed21  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 21
patrol_brique_v34_rdb3_seed22  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 22 --reward root_done_bonus=3.0
patrol_brique_v35_rdb1_seed22  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 22
patrol_brique_v36_rdb3_seed23  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 23 --reward root_done_bonus=3.0
patrol_brique_v37_rdb1_seed23  --scenario patrol_brique --total-steps 3000000 --seed 23
